# A code repeated with different parameters, which is the case that decides whether the reverse
# index may be built from the forward index. The old whole-file scan saw BOTH <A> entries, so
# "+proj=merc +datum=WGS84" reverse-resolves to A, not to B. A reverse index derived from the
# forward map would never have seen A's second parameter set and would answer B.
<A> +proj=longlat +datum=WGS84  <>
<A> +proj=merc +datum=WGS84  <>
<B> +proj=merc +datum=WGS84  <>
<C> +proj=aea +lat_1=50  <>
